%U A262179 -471153005066178699264000000,15434972445968014187888640000000,-92609834675808085127331840000000,161141112335906068121557401600000000,-6923589032624540122910835317145600000000,56496486506216247402952416187908096000000000
%N A262179 Signed denominators of the reduced form of the coefficients of degree 2n terms of the Maclaurin series of (t/sinh(t))^x in t.
%C A262179 Conjecture: this is also the integer sequence A202367 up to sign. These numbers show up in the formula for eigenvectors of Adams operations on the K-theory of unitary groups.
%C A262179 For n >= 1, abs(a(n+1)) is the least common denominator of the coefficients of the polynomial [x^(2*n)](arcsin(x)/x)^r in r; see A401196. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 19 2026
%H A262179 Chi-Kwong Fok, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.01984">Adams operations on classical compact Lie groups</a>, arXiv:1510.01984 [math.AT], 2015-2016.
%H A262179 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/InverseSine.html">Inverse Sine</a>.
%e A262179 p_n(x):=coefficient of t^{2n} of the Maclaurin series of (t/sinh(t))^x
%e A262179 p_0(x)=1
%e A262179 p_1(x)=-x/6
%e A262179 p_2(x)=x(5x+2)/360
%e A262179 p_3(x)=-(35x^3+42x^2+16x)/45360
%e A262179 p_4(x)=(175x^4+420x^3+404x^2+144x)/5443200
%e A262179 p_5(x)=-(385x^5+1540x^4+2684x^3+2288x^2+768x)/359251200
%t A262179 a[n_] := Module[{c}, c = SeriesCoefficient[(t/Sinh[t])^x, {t, 0, 2(n-1)}] // Together; Sign[Numerator[c /. x -> 1]] Denominator[c]];
%t A262179 Table[a[n], {n, 1, 17}] (* Updated by _Jean-François Alcover_, Feb 15 2019 *)
%Y A262179 Cf. A202367 (conjectured absolute values).
%Y A262179 Cf. A401196 (numerator triangle for powers of arcsin(x)/x).
%K A262179 sign,changed
%O A262179 1,2
